-- REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1 (2026-10-20, charter pillar: research; agent_issues 100329, 100326, 100284, 100205, 99913; qnfo-research-exec 0.30.0).
-- REVISE-GUARD-MEASURE-1 (migrations/2026-10-20-revise-guard-measure.sql) set ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard to measure at 2026-10-20 09:38:56Z to stop the reference-clause refusals until the code
-- routes them. This file is the release condition that row names: qnfo-research-exec 0.30.0 applies a revise patch whose only fault is the reference clause and sends the paper to the floor extension
-- (stageComplete, floor-extend) under the guard and under measure alike, so the lever is set back to on and the guard is whole again. Measure had been letting the other two clauses through as well: 11
-- char-floor refusals (2026-10-19T16:34Z to 2026-10-20T07:54Z) would have been applied, and the cut-limit clause is the same. The row is changed by a guarded UPDATE (value on), not deleted: the worker
-- reads only the literal measure, the alternate probe of control research-revise-shrink-guard accepts on, and no BACKUP table is needed.
-- Ordering, stated plainly: this file and the worker deploy run in parallel on merge. For the minutes between them the old 0.29.0 worker sees the guard on and refuses the reference clause again, which is the
-- state of 2026-10-19 (qnfo-audit read 2026-10-20T09:51Z: 374 reference-clause refusals from 14:43Z to 09:31Z, about 20 an hour, and 176 revise-noop in the 12 hours before the lever, about 15 an hour), so a
-- five-minute gap costs about two refused patches and one row sent to the recover path. The new worker does not depend on the row either way (measure no longer disables the route), so no order of the
-- two leaves it inert.
-- Also here (DOCTRINE-1): control research-revise-refs-floor is moved from demote to replace (the refusal is replaced by the floor extension), the new off lever research_revise_refs_extend gets its control row and
-- alternate probe, one decision row is appended, and the closing probe of issue 100329, which a comment containing the issue key satisfied (code-read contains REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1), becomes a d1-query read that
-- is true only when the lever is not measure, a revise-refs-below-floor event routed to the floor extension was logged 60 to 120 minutes ago, and every such event in that window is followed by a floor-extend
-- event on the same row. The failure mode revise-refs-extend-unrestored carries the same read as a detector (expected 0). Windows are minutes, none above 120 (SLA-120M-1).
-- The Rollback restores the lever to measure and removes the control row, its probe, the failure mode and its detector; it leaves the issue contract (the stronger read stays) and decision_log (append-only).
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE ops_config SET value = 'measure', note = 'REVISE-GUARD-MEASURE-1 (2026-10-20): measure restored by the REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1 Rollback. Revert: remove this row (the guard is on when the key is absent).', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE key = 'research_revise_shrink_guard' AND value = 'on'; DELETE FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control = 'research-revise-refs-extend'; DELETE FROM control_registry WHERE control = 'research-revise-refs-extend' AND issue_id = 100329; UPDATE control_registry SET disposition = 'demote' WHERE control = 'research-revise-refs-floor' AND disposition = 'replace' AND issue_id = 99913; DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-revise-refs-extend-unrestored' AND module = 'failure-mode'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'revise-refs-extend-unrestored' AND issue_id = 100329

-- 1. The lever: measure becomes on (the guard). A row at any other value is left alone, so a replay changes nothing.
UPDATE ops_config
SET value = 'on', note = 'REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1 (2026-10-20): the revise shrink guard is back on. qnfo-research-exec 0.30.0 applies a patch whose only fault is the reference clause and routes the paper to the floor extension, under the guard and under measure alike, so measure is no longer needed for that clause, and it applied every patch the char-floor and cut-limit clauses refuse (11 char-floor refusals from 2026-10-19T16:34Z to 2026-10-20T07:54Z). Only the literal value measure changes the worker; on, or an absent key, is the guard. Revert: set this row to measure (REVISE-GUARD-MEASURE-1).', updated_at = datetime('now')
WHERE key = 'research_revise_shrink_guard' AND value = 'measure';

-- 2. The failure mode and its detector: a revise patch was applied and routed to the floor extension, and no extension followed on its row (or the lever was left on measure). Expected 0.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius)
VALUES ('revise-refs-extend-unrestored',
  'a revise patch that took the cited references under the floor was applied and routed to the floor extension, and the extension never ran on its row, so the paper carries fewer references than the floor to review and verify',
  'REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1 applies the patch and relies on stageComplete (floor-extend) to cite the bibliography entries not yet cited. If the extension is switched off, the stage errors, or the row leaves the stage before it runs, the count is not restored; a lever left on measure lets the char-floor and cut-limit clauses through as well',
  'read the row in cloud_ops_events (job qnfo-research-exec) to see why no floor-extend followed (the extension switched off, the stage erroring, the row moved on); ops_config research_revise_refs_extend = off restores the refusal of the reference clause without a deploy; set ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard back to on if it reads measure',
  'the d1-query contract fm-revise-refs-extend-unrestored counts revise-refs-below-floor events routed to the floor extension 60 to 120 minutes ago that have no floor-extend event on the same row, plus one while ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard is measure (expected 0)',
  'fm-revise-refs-extend-unrestored', '2026-10-20', 100329,
  'a revise patch drops a paper under the reference floor and the extension route is not followed by a floor-extend round, or the shrink guard is left on measure',
  'cloud_ops_events kind revise-refs-below-floor with "routed to the floor extension" and no kind floor-extend whose text starts with the same row= token',
  'research-exec papers: a paper with fewer references than the floor reaches review and verify, where gate-refcount holds it; no data loss');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, module, budget_ms, max_items, requires_container, next_due_at)
VALUES ('fm-revise-refs-extend-unrestored', NULL, 'REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1', 'failure-mode detector',
  'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_revise_shrink_guard''), ''on'') = ''measure'' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) + (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cloud_ops_events e WHERE e.job = ''qnfo-research-exec'' AND e.kind = ''revise-refs-below-floor'' AND e.ts <= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-60 minutes'') AND e.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'') AND instr(e.text, ''routed to the floor extension'') > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events f WHERE f.job = ''qnfo-research-exec'' AND f.kind = ''floor-extend'' AND f.ts >= e.ts AND f.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'') AND substr(f.text, 1, instr(f.text, '' '')) = substr(e.text, 1, instr(e.text, '' '')))) AS TEXT) AS observed',
  'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'active', 'failure-mode', 45000, 5, 0, datetime('now'));

-- 3. The closing probe of issue 100329. The class issue-100329 exists (an INSERT OR IGNORE would be ignored), so it is changed in place; the rerun trigger sets it due now. A replay finds the transport already d1-query.
UPDATE remediation_contracts
SET verify_transport = 'd1-query', module = 'refs-extend-closing-v1', status = 'active', attempts = 0, last_verdict = NULL,
  verify_probe = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_revise_shrink_guard''), ''on'') = ''measure'' THEN ''ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard is still measure, so a patch that breaks the char floor or the cut limit is applied'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE job = ''qnfo-research-exec'' AND kind = ''revise-refs-below-floor'' AND ts <= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-60 minutes'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'') AND instr(text, ''routed to the floor extension'') > 0) THEN ''pending: no revise-refs-below-floor event routed to the floor extension between 60 and 120 minutes ago, so the route has not been seen live'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cloud_ops_events e WHERE e.job = ''qnfo-research-exec'' AND e.kind = ''revise-refs-below-floor'' AND e.ts <= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-60 minutes'') AND e.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'') AND instr(e.text, ''routed to the floor extension'') > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events f WHERE f.job = ''qnfo-research-exec'' AND f.kind = ''floor-extend'' AND f.ts >= e.ts AND f.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'') AND substr(f.text, 1, instr(f.text, '' '')) = substr(e.text, 1, instr(e.text, '' '')))) > 0 THEN ''a revise-refs-below-floor event older than 60 minutes has no floor-extend event on its row'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed'
WHERE class = 'issue-100329' AND verify_transport = 'code-read';

-- 4. Controls (DOCTRINE-1). research-revise-refs-floor: demote -> replace, the earlier evidence kept. research-revise-refs-extend: the new off lever, off the critical path, with an alternate probe the chaos drill runs.
UPDATE control_registry
SET disposition = 'replace', alternate_path = 'the floor extension (stageComplete floor-extend, ops_config research_floor_extend) replaces the refusal: a patch whose only fault is the reference clause is applied and the extension cites the bibliography entries not yet cited; the release gate still holds (finalGates gate-length and gate-refcount at verify); ops_config research_revise_refs_extend = off restores the refusal of the reference clause without a deploy; the char-floor and cut-limit clauses stay refusals while research_revise_shrink_guard is not measure',
  evidence = evidence || ' | REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1 (2026-10-20, qnfo-research-exec 0.30.0): disposition demote -> replace; the refusal of the reference clause is replaced by the floor extension in code and the measure lever is set back to on by migrations/2026-10-20-revise-refs-extend.sql (release condition of this row). Closing read: contract issue-100329 and detector fm-revise-refs-extend-unrestored. Alternate probe unchanged: the floor extension must not be switched off.',
  reviewed_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE control = 'research-revise-refs-floor' AND disposition = 'demote';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_registry (control, location, kind, guards_against, critical_path, disposition, disposition_state, alternate_path, evidence, issue_id)
VALUES ('research-revise-refs-extend',
  'qnfo-research-exec stageRevise _applyGuarded / reviseRefsOnly (REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1); ops_config research_revise_refs_extend',
  'kill-switch',
  'the apply-and-extend route repeating a bad deletion: a patch that drops cited references is applied and the floor extension adds a section, so a defect in either could cycle revise, extend and review up to the review-cycle cap (6) on one row, or add sections that cite entries without supporting a claim',
  0, 'keep', 'applied',
  'ops_config research_revise_refs_extend = off restores the refusal of the reference clause without a deploy: a refused patch follows the existing second-model path with the limit stated, and a row that fails all three tries enters the recover path (revise-noop, re-ground) as it did before 2026-10-20; research_floor_extend = off does the same',
  'REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1 (2026-10-20): 374 reference-clause refusals in 19 hours before REVISE-GUARD-MEASURE-1 (qnfo-audit read 09:51Z), each set of three tries a revise-noop and a discarded draft. The route is bounded by the review cycle cap (6) and FLOOR_EXTEND_MAX_ROUNDS (qnfo-research-exec/refs-extend.test.mjs section 3: the delete, extend, review alternation ends in review-hard at cycle 6). Tested alternate: control_alternate_probes row research-revise-refs-extend; the chaos drill stamps alternate_tested_at on a pass.',
  100329);

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_alternate_probes (control, probe_sql, window_note, enabled)
SELECT c.control,
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_revise_refs_extend''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_revise_refs_extend holds a value other than on or off, and only the exact value off switches the route off'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''revise-patch'' AND status IN (''ok'', ''warn'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'')) THEN ''the revise route recorded no revise-patch event in 120 minutes, so the switch guards a route that is not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '120 minutes: a state check on one ops_config key plus the revise route the switch guards, which logs revise-patch about 60 to 100 times an hour; the absent key reads as on',
  1
FROM control_registry c WHERE c.control = 'research-revise-refs-extend';

-- 5. The decision (decision_log is append-only: one row, guarded so a replay adds none).
INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session_01QpQv19uh1padRwZ3u1r766',
  'a revise patch that deletes an unsupported claim and its citation is the right repair for a HARD finding, and the floor extension restores the reference count afterwards, so refusing the patch (or applying it with no extension) wastes the draft; measure on the whole guard is a blunt stand-in that also lets the other two clauses through',
  'REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1: qnfo-research-exec 0.30.0 applies a reference-only revise patch and routes the paper to the floor extension under the guard and under measure; ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard measure -> on (the guard is whole again); control research-revise-refs-floor demote -> replace; control research-revise-refs-extend registered with an alternate probe; failure mode revise-refs-extend-unrestored with its detector; the closing probe of issue 100329 is a d1-query read instead of a code-read for a comment',
  'qnfo-audit read 2026-10-20T09:51Z: 374 reference-clause and 11 char-floor revise-shrink-refused events from 2026-10-19T14:43Z to 2026-10-20T09:31Z, no cut-limit event; 176 revise-noop in the 12 hours before the lever (about 15 an hour); 0 revise-noop since the lever at 09:38:56Z; the lever row still measure; suites qnfo-research-exec/refs-extend.test.mjs (81 checks, measure included) and migrations/revise-refs-extend.test.mjs',
  'applied through the canonical path on merge: the migration sets the lever to on (the worker reads it on its next revise, no deploy) and the worker deploys 0.30.0 beside it; the closing read is probed hourly',
  'one ops_config row, one control row changed and one added with an alternate probe, one failure mode with a detector, one issue contract changed; the revise stage of qnfo-research-exec applies a patch it used to refuse and routes the paper to complete (floor-extend), a decision it now takes on its own; for the minutes between the migration and the deploy the old worker refuses the reference clause again; no secret, schedule or binding change; the gates at verify and publish still hold the reference and length floors',
  'run the migration Rollback header (lever back to measure, control row, probe, failure mode and detector removed, research-revise-refs-floor back to demote) or set ops_config research_revise_refs_extend = off (the refusal of the reference clause returns without a deploy); decision_log is append-only and keeps this row',
  'qnfo-research-exec routes a reference-only revise patch to the floor extension on its own, under the guard as well as under measure',
  'the d1-query contract issue-100329 passes: revise-refs-below-floor events exist after the deploy, every one routed to the floor extension is followed by a floor-extend on its row, ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard is not measure; revise-noop events that name the reference clause stay near 0 while the char-floor and cut-limit clauses refuse again; published papers per day do not fall',
  'papers whose revise used to fail (about 15 an hour entered the recover path) reach review and verify with their references restored instead of being re-grounded; no audience outside the fleet',
  'the worker source and suites (refs-extend.test.mjs sections 2 and 3 run the real stageRevise, stageComplete and stageReview, measure included), the live ops_config row and cloud_ops_events (D1 reads 2026-10-20T09:51Z), control_registry and control_alternate_probes rows, migrations/revise-refs-extend.test.mjs on node:sqlite, scripts/apply_migrations.py --check'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE instr(action, 'REVISE-REFS-EXTEND-1:') = 1);
